  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "# Changes since 0.3.0\n\n            ## Added\n            - **NuGet API key via environment on .NET SDK 10.0.300+** — `publish` now delivers the API key to `dotnet nuget push` through the `NUGET_API_KEY` environment variable on .NET SDK 10.0.300+ (NuGet 7.6), so it never appears on the command line or in the process listing; older .NET SDKs (or an unresponsive probe) fall back to `--api-key`. The .NET SDK probe runs only after every early-exit condition, and printed push lines name the channel, never the key value.\n            - **`dotnet-releaser` migration skill** — `skills/dotnet-releaser-to-releasegen-migration/` guides migrating a dotnet-releaser (TOML) pipeline to ReleaseGen: TOML config inventory, manifest translation, a coverage report, a dry-run validation gate, and a CI rewrite. It is backed by a mapping table that classifies each surface as Mapped, Manual action required, or No ReleaseGen equivalent.\n            - **`releasegen build --rids <rids>`** — a comma-separated subset of the manifest's `runtimeIdentifiers` for the current invocation only (same escape posture as `--preset`): it is never written to the manifest and may only narrow the manifest's declared set, never adding a RID the manifest does not specify. Entries match case-insensitively, de-duplicate, and keep the manifest's spelling; an empty/blank/out-of-set value is refused with a named error before any publish is planned.\n\n            ## Changed\n            - Pinned `Microsoft.Build` package to 18.9.6 since newer versions don't support .NET 10\n            - Dependencies: Meziantou.Analyzer to 3.0.322.\n            - Documentation for commands, stage handoff, and trusted publishing now describes how the API key reaches the spawned push (environment on .NET SDK 10.0.300+, `--api-key` argument otherwise).",
